faq:
  - question: How do you get to Philae Temple in Aswan?
    answer: >-
      Only by boat. Philae is the island Temple of Isis on Agilkia Island, in
      the lake between the two Aswan dams, about twenty minutes' drive south of
      the city. When the rising water threatened it, the temple was moved stone
      by stone to this island, completed in 1980. Your own boat waits on the
      island and brings you back whenever you are ready.
  - question: When should we go?
    answer: >-
      Late morning to early afternoon is the busiest and hottest stretch. Your
